Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: reset SM-X910 PCS before calibration

The Kalama downstream calibration sequence asserts PCS SW_RESET before
programming the tables. Mainline clears this reset but no longer asserts
it on power-off. Test the missing assertion on this board only, without
changing power-off sequencing, timeouts, tables or other PHY variants.

This is a candidate for the intermittent resume PCS_READY timeout, not a
validated fix. Keep out of default builds until offline-root resume tests
pass. qphy_setbits() includes a readback before subsequent table writes.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -1964,6 +1964,12 @@ static int qmp_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct phy *phy)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* SM-X910 experiment: assert PCS reset before calibration tables. */
+	if (cfg == &sm8550_ufsphy_cfg &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9uwifi") &&
+	    !cfg->no_pcs_sw_reset)
+		qphy_setbits(pcs, cfg->regs[QPHY_SW_RESET], SW_RESET);
+
 	qmp_ufs_init_registers(qmp, cfg);
 
 	ret = reset_control_deassert(qmp->ufs_reset);
